{ Now the king and queen mate. A queen cannot mate a king all on her own: your king has to come close and help her. [%csl Gg8,Ge2] }
60... f1=Q+ { He makes a new queen, with check. But she lands right next to your king, and nothing of his guards her. Take her with your king. [%cal Ye2f1] } 61. Kxf1 { Your king eats his new queen and now stands close to his king, guarding the two green squares beside his king. That is the help your queen needs. [%csl Gg1,Gg2] } (61. Ke3 { Your king runs from the check and leaves his new queen alive. } 61... Qg1+ 62. Qxg1+ Kxg1 { The queens came off, and his pawn in the red circle is two steps from a new queen, with your king far away. He is winning. [%csl Rh3] }) (61. Kd2 { Your king steps away from his new queen instead of taking her. } 61... Qg2+ 62. Qxg2+ hxg2 { Both queens are gone, and his pawn in the red circle is one step from making another. He is winning. [%csl Rg2] }) 61... h2 { His pawn walls in his own king. If your move gives no check, he cannot move and is not in check: that is stalemate, a draw. So check him with your queen beside his king, where your king guards her. [%cal Yg8g2] } 62. Qg2# { Mate! Your queen checks right beside his king, and your king guards her, so he cannot take her. That is the king and queen mate: the queen checks, your king guards. [%cal Gf1g2] } (62. Qa8# { Mate as well! Your queen checks from the far corner, and your king covers the two squares beside his king. [%csl Gg1,Gg2] }) (62. Qxe6 { You grab a pawn, but that is not a check, and he has no legal move. That is stalemate, and the game is a draw. [%csl Rh1] }) (62. Kf2 { Your king steps forward, but now he is not in check and cannot move at all. Stalemate: the game ends in a draw. [%csl Rh1] }) (62. Qg1+ { A check, but your queen stands where his pawn can take her. } 62... hxg1=Q+ { His pawn takes your queen and becomes a new queen itself, with check. Now he is the one winning. [%csl Rg1] }) (62. Qh8 { Your queen stares along the edge column at his king, but his own pawn is in the way, so that is no check. He cannot move: stalemate, a draw. [%cal Rh8h2] }) (62. Qg3 { Your queen comes closer, but a queen move with no check leaves him without a single move. Stalemate, and the game is drawn. [%csl Rh1] }) 1-0


