{ You are Black, and his pawn is one step from a new queen. Your queen and king are close to his king. The king and queen mate again: can you find it? }
58. a8=Q { He makes a new queen. It was the only move he had, and it comes too late, because now it is your move. } 58... Qg1+ { Check, right beside his king! Your king guards your queen, so his king cannot take her, and his new queen cannot reach her. [%cal Gf2g1] } (58... Qg2+ { Your king guards your queen there, but his new queen sees that square along the long diagonal. [%cal Ra8g2] } 59. Qxg2+ Ke3 { His new queen took yours, with check. He has the only queen left now, and he is winning. [%csl Rg2] }) (58... Qh3+ { A check right beside his king, but your king is too far away to guard her there. } 59. Kxh3 { His king eats your queen, and his brand new queen is the only one left. [%csl Rh3] }) (58... Qh1+ { A check from the corner, but his new queen is looking straight at that square. [%cal Ra8h1] } 59. Qxh1 { His queen takes yours along the long diagonal, and he is winning now. [%csl Rh1] }) (58... Ke3 { Your king steps away, and that gives his new queen time to start checking. } 59. Qa7+ Ke4 60. Qb7+ { His queen checks you from far away, again and again, and your king cannot hide. It is a draw now. [%csl Rb7] }) 59. Kh3 { His king runs to the only square it has. } 59... Qg3# { Mate! Your queen checks right beside his king, guarded by your king, and his new queen never got to move. That is the king and queen mate. [%cal Gf2g3] } (59... Qg4+ { Your queen checks from beside his king, but your own king cannot reach that square to guard her. } 60. Kxg4 { His king takes your queen, and now only he has one. [%csl Rg4] }) (59... Qg2+ { Your king does guard that square, but his new queen is on the long diagonal and takes. [%cal Ra8g2] } 60. Qxg2+ { His queen took yours, with check, and he is winning. [%csl Rg2] }) (59... Qf1+ { A check from further away, and his king simply walks off the edge column. } 60. Kg4 { His king is out in the open, and his new queen is free to check you. The mate is gone. [%csl Rg4] }) (59... Qh2+ { This check lands beside his king on a square your king cannot reach. } 60. Kxh2 { His king takes her, and his brand new queen now has the board to herself. [%csl Rh2] }) (59... Qh1+ { Your queen checks from the corner, where his new queen can take her along the long diagonal. [%cal Ra8h1] } 60. Qxh1 { His queen captures yours from the far corner, and the game is his. [%csl Rh1] }) 0-1


