[Site "https://lichess.org/analysis/8/8/4P3/8/7p/8/p1K5/k7_b_-_-_0_47"]

{ A pawn race! His king is stuck in the corner, blocking his own pawn, so only his other pawn can move. Yours is two steps from a new queen. }
47... h3 { His pawn runs. It is the only move he has, and now it is racing yours to make a queen. } 48. e7 { Your pawn runs too, one step from a new queen. The race is on. } (48. Kd3 { Your king walks off to chase his pawn, and that lets his king out of the corner. } 48... Kb2 49. e7 a1=Q 50. e8=Q { His king got out, his corner pawn became a queen first, and it is his move. He is winning now. [%csl Ra1] }) (48. Kb3 { Your king goes after the pawn beside his king, but that frees a square, and his king walks out of the corner. } 48... Kb1 49. e7 a1=Q 50. e8=Q Qb2+ { He made a queen first and is checking your king, and the race is his. [%csl Rb2] }) 48... h2 { His pawn is one step away as well, but it is your move. } 49. e8=Q { A new queen! His pawn is one step from a queen too, and his king is still stuck in the corner. } (49. Kd2 { Your king steps away before making the queen, and that gives his king a square. } 49... h1=Q 50. e8=Q { Now you both have a queen, and his king has room to breathe. The mate is gone and the game is a draw. [%csl Rb2] }) 49... h1=Q { He makes a new queen as well, so it is queen against queen. But it is your move. } 50. Qe5# { Mate! Your queen checks along the long diagonal, your king covers the two squares beside his king, and his own pawn blocks the last one. The king and queen mate wins the race. [%cal Ge5a1][%csl Gb1,Gb2] } (50. Qe1+ { A check, but his new queen stands on the same row and takes yours. [%cal Rh1e1] } 50... Qxe1 { His queen took yours, and now he is winning. [%csl Re1] }) (50. Qh8+ { A check along the long diagonal, but his new queen is looking straight along the edge column at that square. [%cal Rh1h8] } 50... Qxh8 { His queen took yours along the edge column, and the game has turned around. [%csl Rh8] }) (50. Qe6 { A queen move with no check, and his new queen starts checking your king. } 50... Qb1+ 51. Kc3 Qc1+ 52. Kd3 { Your king had to step away from his, his king has room now, and his queen can keep checking. It is a draw. [%csl Rb2] }) (50. Qe4 { Your queen attacks his, but she stands on his queen's diagonal, and he takes first, with check. [%cal Rh1e4] } 50... Qxe4+ { His queen captured yours with check, and your king is left alone against a queen. [%csl Re4] }) 1-0


