{ His king is boxed in by his own pawns already. There is a smothered mate here in two moves. Can you find the first one? } 36. Ka1 { He hides his king in the corner beside his own two pawns, which leaves it exactly one free square to run to. } Qc1+ { You offer your queen for free right in front of his king. Nothing of his can take her, so he has to block on that one free square. } (36... Nxd3 { Your knight grabs a pawn and forgets his king. That hands him the time he needs to start checking you. } 37. Qc6+ Kd8 38. Qd6+ Ke8 39. Qe6+ { His queen chases your king from check to check and you can never get away from her. The mate has turned into a draw. }) (36... Qd2 { Your queen steps somewhere safe and stops attacking anything at all. His queen starts checking straight away. } 37. Qc6+ Kd8 38. Qd6+ Ke8 39. Qe6+ { He checks you from one side and then the other, and your king can never hide. A mate in two has become half a point. }) (36... Qb3 { Your queen lands on a square his pawn and his queen both attack, with nothing of yours guarding her. He takes her for free. } 37. Qxb3 Kd8 38. Qe6 Nc2+ 39. Kb1 { You are a whole queen down and his king has strolled out of the corner. There is nothing left for you to attack. }) 37. Nb1 { He has to block with his knight, and now his own knight and his own two pawns fill every single square around his king. } Nc2# { Mate! Your knight checks him and your queen guards it from behind, while his own knight and pawns block every escape. A smothered mate. [%csl Ra1,Gb1,Ga2,Gb2] } (37... Qxb1+ { Your queen takes the knight with check, but that knight was the wall that trapped him. His king takes back and steps free. } 38. Kxb1 Nf3 39. Qc6+ Kd8 40. Qb6+ { You are a queen down for a knight and his queen just checks you over and over. The mate is gone for good. }) (37... Nxd3 { Your knight has exactly one square that mates and this is not it. Here his queen simply takes it off the board. } 38. Qxd3 Qh1 39. Qf5+ Kb8 { Your knight went for one pawn and cost you a piece, and his king has walked out of the corner to safety. }) (37... Qe3 { A quiet queen move with a mate sitting right there on the board. He gets a free move to rescue his king. } 38. Qc6+ Kd8 39. a3 Qe5 { His king has walked out of the corner into open space and nothing you have can catch it. The game is level again. }) 0-1


